      "id": "def-ordinal",
      "concern": "The order-type remark says the equivalence class of the empty well-order is the singleton {∅}. Under def-well-order, a well-order is the pair (W,≤), so this class is {(∅,∅)}, rather than {∅}. The proper-class comparison remains correct, but the singleton description needs to identify its coding convention.",
